1
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,239
I heard

2
00:01:39,519 --> 00:01:42,840
you're very close with mainland officials.

3
00:01:43,359 --> 00:01:44,959
Under Section Chief Zhu's directives,

4
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,480
in Minzhong, I mainly focused on

5
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:47,480
befriending the higher-ups.

6
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,359
Party, government, military, and business—

7
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:49,560
I have brothers across all of them.

8
00:01:51,879 --> 00:01:53,799
What about mainland state security?

9
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:55,920
Any contact with them?

10
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,239
No.

11
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,719
Inside our agency,

12
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:03,920
there's a bounty.

13
00:02:04,159 --> 00:02:05,599
A reward, really.

14
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:07,040
Whoever

15
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:11,120
can secure a clear photo of Minzhong State Security

16
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:13,199
Bureau Chief Wu Shenglai

17
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,879
gets a ten million reward.

18
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,159
Are you confident?

19
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:26,159
No.

20
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,840
Really no confidence?

21
00:02:30,319 --> 00:02:30,800
No.

22
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,639
You answered quickly.

23
00:02:48,439 --> 00:02:49,680
Got promoted and changed your attitude, huh?

24
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,960
Can't even joke with you anymore, right?

25
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:52,599
Let me tell you,

26
00:02:52,599 --> 00:02:54,360
watch how you talk to me in here from now on.

27
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,039
This building is all about discipline now.

28
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,800
It's no place for joking around.

29
00:03:03,719 --> 00:03:06,319
I didn't even know you were back, okay?

30
00:03:07,599 --> 00:03:08,639
If I weren't giving you a polygraph test,

31
00:03:08,639 --> 00:03:09,960
I wouldn't even know you were back today.

32
00:03:10,719 --> 00:03:11,560
Cut the crap.

33
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,280
Where are you treating me to dinner and drinks tonight?

34
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,479
Me treat? You're treating!

35
00:03:14,479 --> 00:03:15,439
Come on, you're treating!

36
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:28,039
Come on, stop it.

37
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,479
What do you mean?

38
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:30,159
What?

39
00:03:30,159 --> 00:03:30,879
What are we eating?

40
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,360
There's this place.

41
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:34,599
Unprecedented in the past,

42
00:03:34,599 --> 00:03:35,599
unmatched in the future.

43
00:03:38,319 --> 00:03:39,000
Old Zhu.

44
00:03:40,039 --> 00:03:41,039
What do you think?

45
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,120
He hasn't seen many big shots.

46
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,080
It's natural he was nervous meeting you.

47
00:03:48,319 --> 00:03:49,080
Actually,

48
00:03:49,919 --> 00:03:51,719
he did accomplish quite a bit on the mainland.

49
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,360
Unlike those who just talk big.

50
00:03:53,599 --> 00:03:56,199
Xie Fengshi isn't a big shot?

51
00:03:57,159 --> 00:03:58,159
How big does someone have to be?

52
00:03:58,719 --> 00:04:00,000
Can he even reach that high?

53
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,719
Sometimes,

54
00:04:02,039 --> 00:04:04,080
planning ahead is the way to go.

55
00:04:04,879 --> 00:04:07,479
Xie will get promoted eventually.

56
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,280
And his whole line will move up with him.

57
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,879
Seeds sprout,

58
00:04:11,879 --> 00:04:13,479
saplings grow into big trees.

59
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,639
By that time,

60
00:04:16,639 --> 00:04:18,079
we'll be ready to retire.

61
00:04:24,319 --> 00:04:26,319
Following me back like this,

62
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,199
you must want something.

63
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,800
Just speak your mind.

64
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,839
Getting more and more hypocritical.

65
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,399
Just like me.

66
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:38,360
Out with it.

67
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,879
Good news or bad news?

68
00:04:42,079 --> 00:04:44,439
I'd only bring it up here if it were good.

69
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,439
My mole over there needs funds.

70
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,600
The request was submitted long ago,

71
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,439
but it keeps getting held up.

72
00:04:49,439 --> 00:04:51,480
I'm hoping to fast-track it.

73
00:04:51,879 --> 00:04:53,040
Just tell me how much.

74
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:53,920
Same as last time.

75
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,519
Such heavy expenses.

76
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,560
That's a good thing, too.

77
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,199
You can't get intel without spending big.

78
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,439
We run a casino.

79
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,480
Just waiting for people to slip up.

80
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,480
That's what you said.

81
00:05:06,519 --> 00:05:07,240
Leave it on the table.

82
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,800
The game's over, why haven't you left?

83
00:05:19,839 --> 00:05:21,439
Lin Kanshan and his crew,

84
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,959
worked their hearts out undercover on the mainland.

85
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,800
Shouldn't we pick an example to commend?

86
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,680
To set a standard for everyone.

87
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:31,160
Even if we do, it wouldn't be him.

88
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:32,639
He's been at the table so long,

89
00:05:32,879 --> 00:05:35,839
let alone Big 3 Dragons or Small 4 Winds,

90
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,800
he hasn't even drawn a winning tile.

91
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,360
At most, he gets a chicken hand.

92
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:40,680
Commend him for what?

93
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:44,920
We'll send him to Europe in a while.

94
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,519
Who knows?

95
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:47,879
With a win on a kong,

96
00:05:47,879 --> 00:05:48,920
he might draw a winning hand.

97
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,519
More like a bloom on his ass.

98
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,920
Wait till you actually draw it.

99
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:52,560
You...

100
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,279
Aren't you talking about yourself?

101
00:05:57,519 --> 00:06:00,120
Still, that medicine you gave me really worked.

102
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,079
Right?

103
00:06:01,279 --> 00:06:01,720
Yeah.

104
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,199
I can finally sit down in peace.

105
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,160
Exactly.

106
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,040
Is this what you were talking about?

107
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:20,920
Let's go.

108
00:06:23,199 --> 00:06:25,839
I'll lead the way. This way, please.

109
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,759
Intelligence Center,

110
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,279
Assistant Director

111
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:50,959
Chen Leyuan!

112
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:53,319
Don't think I didn't know.

113
00:06:53,959 --> 00:06:55,560
A promotion is great news.

114
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,720
Why keep it from me?

115
00:06:57,519 --> 00:06:59,079
You're still just slacking off there.

116
00:06:59,079 --> 00:07:00,920
Even a rock could sit there and do the job.

117
00:07:01,199 --> 00:07:02,959
I'm an assistant director, okay?

118
00:07:03,279 --> 00:07:05,360
An assistant, not the director.

119
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,279
Just kiss the right asses and you're good.

120
00:07:07,279 --> 00:07:08,959
I ran my legs off on the mainland,

121
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:12,399
yet it doesn't beat serving hot tea here.

122
00:07:12,639 --> 00:07:14,519
That guy who always brings files to Zheng Guiping,

123
00:07:14,519 --> 00:07:15,319
what does he know?

124
00:07:15,319 --> 00:07:16,480
Tell me, what does he know?

125
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,720
He's already about to be promoted to deputy team leader.

126
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:20,279
Let me tell you,

127
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:22,360
not many people are as foolish as us.

128
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,120
You have to know how to work the system.

129
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,360
Even if you don't climb the ladder, you can still make money.

130
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,959
Do you know how they do it?

131
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,399
They go to the mainland from Matsu

132
00:07:34,639 --> 00:07:35,560
to buy a paper, touch it up a bit,

133
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,639
and boom, it turns into intelligence.

134
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,759
They get whatever bonus they ask for.

135
00:07:39,759 --> 00:07:42,480
Why go to the mainland to fake intel?

136
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:45,839
Like that "Ronghai Garrison Bureau"—

137
00:07:45,839 --> 00:07:47,360
it's completely fabricated out of thin air!

138
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,319
There's no such department!

139
00:07:49,439 --> 00:07:51,240
Come on, at least give me some real intel,

140
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:51,759
will you?

141
00:07:51,759 --> 00:07:52,720
That's impossible.

142
00:07:52,879 --> 00:07:55,000
I've run polygraph tests for years.

143
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,360
Why is it impossible?

144
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:58,399
You're just too honest, okay?

145
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,439
Everyone else is just scamming

146
00:07:59,439 --> 00:08:00,439
and playing each other for fools.

147
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,879
There's an even more ridiculous one.

148
00:08:03,079 --> 00:08:05,319
Rumor has it the director's nephew

149
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:06,720
was sent to the mainland to pad his resume.

150
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,319
He does have intel,

151
00:08:08,959 --> 00:08:10,040
but he splits it into pieces.

152
00:08:10,279 --> 00:08:11,959
When reporting to headquarters,

153
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:14,519
who knows if he really has informants,

154
00:08:14,519 --> 00:08:16,560
but he claims bonuses per head.

155
00:08:16,879 --> 00:08:18,600
They give him whatever he asks for.

156
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,160
You can even do that?

157
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,439
We really are...

158
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,439
We're making less and less money.

159
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,639
I'd make more driving a cab.

160
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,199
So many people want to quit right now.

161
00:08:28,319 --> 00:08:30,000
Let me tell you, next time you come back,

162
00:08:30,439 --> 00:08:31,639
I might just...

163
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:33,840
Cut the crap.

164
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:34,600
Really.

165
00:08:35,279 --> 00:08:37,039
Right now, you're the one with boundless prospects.

166
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:38,519
Boundless prospects my ass.

167
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:39,559
Here's to you,

168
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:40,240
Chen Boundless.

169
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:41,080
Screw off.

170
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:46,879
I heard...

171
00:08:47,759 --> 00:08:49,519
isn't Old Zhu in bad shape?

172
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:50,799
High blood sugar.

173
00:08:50,799 --> 00:08:51,799
He fainted twice.

174
00:08:51,879 --> 00:08:52,960
Is he about to retire?

175
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:55,159
That news has even reached the mainland?

176
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:56,279
What do you think?

177
00:08:56,679 --> 00:08:57,759
Then who's going to oversee us?

178
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,279
I heard

179
00:09:01,679 --> 00:09:04,279
isn't he locking horns with Liqing?

180
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,639
When you step down, I step up.

181
00:09:10,879 --> 00:09:11,960
Liqing...

182
00:09:12,559 --> 00:09:13,919
isn't so bad, actually.

183
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,360
What do you mean?

184
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:24,519
Chen Shui-bian is seeking re-election as mayor.

185
00:09:24,519 --> 00:09:26,799
Everyone's betting on whether he can pull it off.

186
00:09:26,799 --> 00:09:27,639
What if...

187
00:09:28,519 --> 00:09:30,000
I mean, just what if...

188
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,080
If the DPP

189
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,679
becomes the "ruling party,"

190
00:09:34,559 --> 00:09:35,799
would someone like Chen Shui-bian,

191
00:09:35,799 --> 00:09:38,000
a former prisoner and dissident,

192
00:09:38,639 --> 00:09:40,559
turn around and take revenge on us?

193
00:09:46,679 --> 00:09:47,679
Who cares?

194
00:09:48,039 --> 00:09:49,279
Maybe we'll wake up

195
00:09:51,039 --> 00:09:51,799
and we'll be reunified.

196
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:58,120
Then we'd have to attend the People's Congress!

197
00:09:58,519 --> 00:09:59,120
Drink!

198
00:09:59,200 --> 00:09:59,799
Come on!

199
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:01,120
Here's to you, Boundless!

200
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,240
Give her a call.

201
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,159
Won't I see her when I get home soon?

202
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:19,559
You know how impatient your wife is.

203
00:10:19,879 --> 00:10:21,200
The more you stall, the more anxious she gets.

204
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,080
Just play your chess.

205
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:24,840
If she asks,

206
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,440
tell her we're in a meeting at the provincial department.

207
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,559
What's the big hassle?

208
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:30,320
Why not just take care of it?

209
00:10:30,519 --> 00:10:31,279
My wife...

210
00:10:31,279 --> 00:10:32,240
for several days straight,

211
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,799
her late grandmother visited her dreams.

212
00:10:34,799 --> 00:10:35,759
Yet she won't say what she wants.

213
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,440
Her dad consulted a fortune teller,

214
00:10:37,759 --> 00:10:39,799
who said the departed wants something.

215
00:10:40,039 --> 00:10:41,200
Still didn't say what it is.

216
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,279
Now she wants me to figure it out.

217
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,320
What am I supposed to do?

218
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,360
Well, you have to play along.

219
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:45,679
That depends on what it is.

220
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,360
How can I play along with this?

221
00:10:47,639 --> 00:10:48,279
I'm a Party member.

222
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,679
Forget it, it'll blow over in a couple days.

223
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,879
I just won't listen to her nagging.

224
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,679
Isn't it because you're the most capable?

225
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:55,759
The departed always seek out someone

226
00:10:55,759 --> 00:10:57,080
who can actually solve their problems.

227
00:10:57,399 --> 00:10:58,559
Nobody in my family comes to me in dreams.

228
00:10:59,039 --> 00:10:59,799
For things like this,

229
00:10:59,919 --> 00:11:01,639
the ancestors go to my brother-in-law.

230
00:11:02,159 --> 00:11:03,039
Good for your ancestors.

231
00:11:03,279 --> 00:11:04,759
They know you're busy working overtime.

232
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:05,759
As if I'm not busy?

233
00:11:06,159 --> 00:11:07,960
As long as your wife is retired and free, it's fine.

234
00:11:08,159 --> 00:11:09,600
Once elders cross to the other side,

235
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:10,720
they see everything clearly.

236
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,320
Just like what those spies are up to,

237
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,519
we know it all in our hearts.

238
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,440
Wen Zongshu, Lin Kanshan...

239
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:16,919
Whether they're truly busy or just faking it,

240
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,799
isn't it all crystal clear to you?

241
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,399
If Lin Kanshan hadn't run,

242
00:11:21,519 --> 00:11:22,600
we wouldn't have known Wen Zongshu

243
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:23,519
was walking the same path.

244
00:11:24,519 --> 00:11:25,200
That's fine too.

245
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,600
Let's keep this fish in the pond for now.

246
00:11:27,279 --> 00:11:28,200
Believe it or not,

247
00:11:28,279 --> 00:11:30,559
this Boss Lin will definitely return.

248
00:11:31,159 --> 00:11:32,000
If I were him,

249
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:32,879
I'd come back too.

250
00:11:33,879 --> 00:11:35,039
How is Jin Lina doing?

251
00:11:35,759 --> 00:11:36,519
She's not being straight with us.

252
00:11:36,759 --> 00:11:37,960
Everything she says is a lie.

253
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:38,919
Being dishonest isn't necessarily bad.

254
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,480
We can just read between the lines in reverse.

255
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:43,559
As for Li Fengge connecting with her,

256
00:11:44,159 --> 00:11:45,559
let's leave that to time.

257
00:11:45,559 --> 00:11:46,519
Speaking of Li Fengge,

258
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,679
your Second Division's

259
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,200
cadre promotion list

260
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,720
and the reserve talent roster

261
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,159
passed the Party committee meeting today.

262
00:11:53,639 --> 00:11:54,480
Did she give it to you?

263
00:11:54,639 --> 00:11:56,360
I just got back from a business trip and haven't seen her yet.

264
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,799
Who ended up making the talent roster?

265
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:01,039
Check!

266
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:04,720
I didn't see that! Didn't see it!

267
00:12:04,919 --> 00:12:05,799
Come on, let's both take back one move.

268
00:12:05,919 --> 00:12:06,799
No take-backs!

269
00:12:07,279 --> 00:12:08,120
Let's play another game.

270
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:39,720
I'm done, Sis.

271
00:12:40,399 --> 00:12:40,960
Don't waste it.

272
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:41,399
Take the egg with you.

273
00:12:41,399 --> 00:12:42,080
I'm finished, Sis Li.

274
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:42,919
Did you pack it up?

275
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,120
Just focus on your food.

276
00:12:44,879 --> 00:12:46,159
Always bringing boiled eggs home.

277
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:47,960
How much can a few buns really save?

278
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:49,519
Grabbing two cartons of milk would be much better.

279
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,480
If you don't finish in the morning, it can do for lunch.

280
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,159
Right?

281
00:12:52,159 --> 00:12:53,039
It's just less hassle.

282
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,320
You just love pinching pennies.

283
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,120
Both she and her husband are cops.

284
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:08,279
Her husband is overseas all year round,

285
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:11,320
she cares for the elders and kid alone.

286
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,600
How would she have time to cook?

287
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:14,440
Not everyone can be as carefree as you guys.

288
00:13:15,879 --> 00:13:16,919
Just eat your food,

289
00:13:16,919 --> 00:13:18,240
and keep your mouths shut.

290
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,519
Look. Don't they look alike?

291
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,559
Look at how he holds his chopsticks,

292
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:35,000
and the way he eats date cake.

293
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,159
He really does.

294
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,720
Alike? Like who?

295
00:13:40,919 --> 00:13:42,320
It's not just the way he eats.

296
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,679
Even his investigative thinking,

297
00:13:43,679 --> 00:13:45,759
and his catchphrase, right?

298
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:47,960
Now that you mention it,

299
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,600
from this angle,

300
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,240
I think they even look more and more alike.

301
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,480
Look at the eyes and brows.

302
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:55,320
When two people spend that much time together,

303
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,080
they can actually start resembling each other.

304
00:13:57,799 --> 00:13:59,840
It's okay to learn other things from him,

305
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,639
just don't copy his love life.

306
00:14:01,639 --> 00:14:03,399
He juggles multiple girlfriends non-stop.

307
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,039
Do I really take after him that much?

308
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:08,879
Does he really have that many girlfriends?

309
00:14:08,879 --> 00:14:09,759
Let me count them for you.

310
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,720
Let me tell you about this...

311
00:14:11,879 --> 00:14:12,320
Brother Qi—

312
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:14,159
Morning, Brother Qi.

313
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:14,559
Morning.

314
00:14:14,559 --> 00:14:16,080
How are you always right on time?

315
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:17,519
Not a minute early, not a second late.

316
00:14:17,519 --> 00:14:18,399
How do you do it?

317
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:19,840
I have to visit the hospital.

318
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,200
Daytime hours are unpredictable,

319
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:23,000
so I have to time it during doctor rounds.

320
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,080
Whether I'm on time for work

321
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,639
now depends on the ward's schedule.

322
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,360
How's the old lady doing now?

323
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,840
Could be better, could be worse.

324
00:14:33,879 --> 00:14:34,679
Such dark circles under your eyes.

325
00:14:35,279 --> 00:14:36,240
Didn't sleep well again?

326
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,600
Every night now,

327
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,960
I have to mentally replay everything

328
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,000
that happened during the day.

329
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,039
My brain is working overtime,

330
00:14:42,039 --> 00:14:43,159
so I can't fall asleep at all.

331
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,960
Got any good tips?

332
00:14:47,679 --> 00:14:49,519
I heard about a method to fall asleep fast.

333
00:14:49,519 --> 00:14:51,480
It takes just 20 seconds to reach deep sleep.

334
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:52,159
For real?

335
00:14:52,159 --> 00:14:53,039
You have to train for it.

336
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,240
Train yourself to doze off at red lights,

337
00:14:55,399 --> 00:14:56,840
catch up on sleep on the bus,

338
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:57,919
squeeze in a nap whenever you can.

339
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,519
That's tough. How do you train for that?

340
00:14:59,519 --> 00:15:00,519
If you can't, that's on you.

341
00:15:00,919 --> 00:15:01,480
Pop quiz.

342
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,679
When is daytime sleep the sweetest?

343
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,759
When?

344
00:15:06,159 --> 00:15:06,919
During meetings.

345
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:24,080
Is Cao Liaoping being sentenced today?

346
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:25,120
At 10:30 AM.

347
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:26,240
It's already started.

348
00:15:26,799 --> 00:15:28,360
As for the new leads that came up,

349
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,639
we still need to pursue them.

350
00:15:29,639 --> 00:15:30,960
But regardless,

351
00:15:31,519 --> 00:15:32,639
Cao's case is solved,

352
00:15:33,039 --> 00:15:34,240
and our Second Division

353
00:15:34,679 --> 00:15:36,240
didn't lose face.

354
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,080
Otherwise,

355
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,759
I'd be too embarrassed to ask for

356
00:15:38,759 --> 00:15:40,440
our section-chief level promotion quota.

357
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,840
Following standard procedures,

358
00:15:43,039 --> 00:15:45,720
via careful vetting and open nominations,

359
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:46,679
including

360
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:47,799
reviewing personnel files,

361
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,200
verifying background information,

362
00:15:50,519 --> 00:15:52,440
and drafting promotion criteria,

363
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,679
the Bureau Party Committee

364
00:15:54,679 --> 00:15:56,240
discussed and determined that

365
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:58,200
the section-chief level candidate is

366
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,840
Comrade Yin Baoshan.

367
00:16:13,159 --> 00:16:14,480
Director Wei, I can't do it.

368
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,720
I don't deserve this.

369
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,080
Ma Qi is far more qualified than me.

370
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,440
You should give it to Brother Qi.

371
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,679
The vetting process will follow regulations.

372
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:24,240
Next is the reserve talent promotion list,

373
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:26,320
with one spot for each division.

374
00:16:26,639 --> 00:16:29,679
Besides the strict age requirement,

375
00:16:29,679 --> 00:16:32,279
candidates are mainly evaluated on

376
00:16:32,279 --> 00:16:33,720
character, skills, diligence, and results.

377
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,000
Based on all of this,

378
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,399
and with the organization's approval,

379
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,960
the Second Division's reserve candidate

380
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,639
is Comrade Ding Xiaohe.

381
00:16:44,039 --> 00:16:45,039
Me?

382
00:16:45,039 --> 00:16:46,039
Let's give them a round of applause.

383
00:17:11,119 --> 00:17:12,000
Meeting adjourned, everyone.

384
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,839
Director Wei, I really don't think I'm up for this.

385
00:17:14,839 --> 00:17:16,640
I strongly recommend Ma Qi.

386
00:17:16,839 --> 00:17:17,480
Let's go, let's go.

387
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,880
The meeting is already over.

388
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,519
I haven't adjourned the meeting yet,

389
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,839
and you run out to take a leak.

390
00:17:33,839 --> 00:17:34,400
That's hardly appropriate, is it?

391
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,519
Hesitancy. Occupational hazard.

392
00:17:36,839 --> 00:17:38,319
Once the urge hits, I have to rush.

393
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,480
Don't try to brush me off with that.

394
00:17:40,799 --> 00:17:42,119
I put in an application for you.

395
00:17:42,119 --> 00:17:43,240
The higher-ups turned it down.

396
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:45,000
You know the promotion criteria.

397
00:17:45,359 --> 00:17:46,720
Competence alone isn't enough.

398
00:17:47,079 --> 00:17:48,039
No need to apply on my behalf.

399
00:17:48,319 --> 00:17:48,799
If you think

400
00:17:48,799 --> 00:17:50,759
I'm upset Baoshan made section-chief,

401
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:52,640
then you're really selling me short.

402
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,079
Almost forgot.

403
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,799
Congrats on your promotion to deputy bureau chief.

404
00:17:57,799 --> 00:17:59,279
I'll have to call you Chief Wei from now on.

405
00:17:59,279 --> 00:18:00,319
Cut the crap.

406
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,400
As if I don't know you're holding a grudge.

407
00:18:02,839 --> 00:18:04,000
Don't end up like Cao Liaoping.

408
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,440
You have to let it go.

409
00:18:07,279 --> 00:18:08,160
To put it bluntly,

410
00:18:08,319 --> 00:18:10,440
I wouldn't care even if they made me division chief.

411
00:18:10,799 --> 00:18:12,680
The MIB put a bounty on our photos.

412
00:18:12,799 --> 00:18:14,000
Do you know how much you're worth?

413
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:14,839
Or Baoshan?

414
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:17,519
Yang Shiwen said I'm worth more than you.

415
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:19,079
Still, it's different for the young folks.

416
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,319
Especially those who've been wronged.

417
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:23,799
I knew you were speaking up for He Chunxiao.

418
00:18:24,119 --> 00:18:24,839
Go on, keep venting.

419
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:26,920
Is it because he and Jinlan

420
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:28,039
were almost exposed in Hong Kong, China?

421
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:30,920
If so, we might as well just sit in the office.

422
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,000
None of us should go on field ops anymore.

423
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,079
I know that

424
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:35,279
my meeting with him in Hong Kong, China

425
00:18:35,279 --> 00:18:36,920
will definitely affect my promotion.

426
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:38,119
I don't care about myself.

427
00:18:38,279 --> 00:18:39,240
But here's a question:

428
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:42,400
If an ordinary citizen targeted by a spy

429
00:18:42,759 --> 00:18:45,000
makes a mistake unwittingly—

430
00:18:45,079 --> 00:18:47,359
say, while being single,

431
00:18:47,759 --> 00:18:49,599
with a US or Taiwan, China intel officer,

432
00:18:49,599 --> 00:18:51,079
he gets involved and sleeps with her,

433
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:53,400
and then reports it proactively to his agency,

434
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:55,319
assuming his agency handles secrets—

435
00:18:55,319 --> 00:18:57,480
if he is still punished in a case like that,

436
00:18:57,920 --> 00:19:00,400
won't that discourage people from coming forward?

437
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:02,079
Is that really beneficial to national security?

438
00:19:03,359 --> 00:19:05,279
On one hand, you urge targeted individuals

439
00:19:05,279 --> 00:19:06,920
to step forward and report.

440
00:19:07,359 --> 00:19:09,359
On the other, you discipline or sideline them.

441
00:19:09,799 --> 00:19:11,240
Who will ever report voluntarily after that?

442
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:13,079
It's the same for Chunxiao and Jinlan.

443
00:19:13,079 --> 00:19:14,400
When it comes to selecting young talent,

444
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,480
it's simply unfair.

445
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,519
If you don't push for He Chunxiao,

446
00:19:16,519 --> 00:19:17,839
no one will accept the outcome.

447
00:19:17,839 --> 00:19:19,640
Even Ding Xiaohe feels awkward about it.

448
00:19:19,759 --> 00:19:21,599
If any slip-up on a mission docks points,

449
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:23,440
how can we expect anyone to risk it all?

450
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,759
Is this your first day on the job?

451
00:19:27,039 --> 00:19:29,799
Can an individual dictate state laws?

452
00:19:29,799 --> 00:19:31,400
Fine, fine. I get it. Say no more.

453
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,839
Just take your leak in peace, Chief.

454
00:19:38,119 --> 00:19:39,759
What kind of tea do you usually like?

455
00:19:39,759 --> 00:19:41,079
Rougui or white tea?

456
00:19:42,599 --> 00:19:44,519
Director Wei, I usually drink soft drinks.

457
00:19:44,519 --> 00:19:46,279
I rarely drink tea.

458
00:19:48,799 --> 00:19:49,440
No rush.

459
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:52,799
Once you reach a certain age,

460
00:19:52,799 --> 00:19:54,039
your taste will change naturally.

461
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:55,079
Thank you.

462
00:19:56,119 --> 00:19:57,400
Don't think it's that far off.

463
00:19:58,440 --> 00:19:59,880
Maybe before long,

464
00:20:00,119 --> 00:20:02,000
you'll be sneaking over to steal my tea.

465
00:20:03,519 --> 00:20:04,519
As for the listening post,

466
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:07,079
we can't dismantle it just yet.

467
00:20:07,359 --> 00:20:09,720
What you and Jinlan do day to day

468
00:20:09,839 --> 00:20:11,039
will be assigned later.

469
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:13,079
Just go about your work as usual.

470
00:20:13,279 --> 00:20:14,839
Who knows, one day when you get home,

471
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:17,119
that neighbor of yours might just be back.

472
00:20:19,319 --> 00:20:20,039
Understood.

473
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:21,720
In case Lin Kanshan comes back,

474
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,480
everything stays business as usual.

475
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:23,160
Right.

476
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:24,839
That includes you and Ma Qi.

477
00:20:25,039 --> 00:20:26,200
Earn money as you should,

478
00:20:26,319 --> 00:20:27,240
and socialize as you should.

479
00:20:27,359 --> 00:20:29,119
If you two have what it takes

480
00:20:29,119 --> 00:20:30,240
to grow the company,

481
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:31,359
and maybe even take it public,

482
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,480
it'll give the brass a pleasant surprise.

483
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:36,960
Honestly, I've had trouble sleeping,

484
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:39,200
worried we might run it into bankruptcy.

485
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:42,839
As for the reserve cadre list,

486
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:44,519
the reasons are quite complicated.

487
00:20:44,519 --> 00:20:46,400
If Lin Kanshan never comes back,

488
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,359
how will Brother Qi and I be assigned?

489
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,279
He'll be given other assignments.

490
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,000
If your assistance is needed,

491
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,440
the division will let you know.

492
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:57,079
However, you need to prepare yourself mentally

493
00:20:57,319 --> 00:20:59,079
to handle things completely on your own.

494
00:20:59,359 --> 00:21:01,119
You can't be an apprentice forever.

495
00:21:01,359 --> 00:21:02,720
Everyone has to graduate at some point.

496
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:05,279
Maybe much sooner than you think.

497
00:21:09,279 --> 00:21:11,119
New shoes, a new path.

498
00:21:12,759 --> 00:21:13,839
What's the occasion?

499
00:21:16,599 --> 00:21:17,640
I just wanted to buy them.

500
00:21:19,279 --> 00:21:20,519
I just wanted to wear them.

501
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:22,960
I just had to wear them.

502
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:43,279
Give it to me. Give it to me.

503
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:52,519
If you want to cry, just let it out.

504
00:21:54,359 --> 00:21:55,200
It's okay.

505
00:21:55,799 --> 00:21:57,200
Can you eat something first, then?

506
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:11,279
Then tell me,

507
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,400
have you found any new leads lately?

508
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:35,000
You think he'll marry you and protect you?

509
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,519
It's just a pair of shoes.

510
00:22:36,799 --> 00:22:38,000
If you like them,

511
00:22:38,319 --> 00:22:39,240
I'll give them to you.

512
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:40,680
Who owes whom, really?

513
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:42,279
Everywhere we go, you make money off me.

514
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:44,000
I pay your salary during the day,

515
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,960
and tip you when we go singing at night.

516
00:22:46,279 --> 00:22:48,000
Just who is whose... whose...

517
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,000
whose boss, anyway?

518
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,960
He just doesn't have a wife here.

519
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:52,799
How do you know he doesn't have one in Taiwan, China?

520
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:54,960
I'm trying to save you right now.

521
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:21,960
Are you specifically giving me a ride home,

522
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:23,119
or do you have something to say?

523
00:23:25,079 --> 00:23:26,240
Why wait at the gate?

524
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:27,519
Couldn't you wait in the courtyard?

525
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:31,079
You stood up for me today,

526
00:23:31,079 --> 00:23:32,319
so I'm driving you home tonight.

527
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:34,160
I was afraid it might look bad for you.

528
00:23:36,359 --> 00:23:38,119
You mean look bad for yourself.

529
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:40,440
Where are you going today? Headed home?

530
00:23:42,359 --> 00:23:43,799
Take me to the Provincial People's Hospital.

531
00:23:51,359 --> 00:23:52,839
Who said I stood up for you?

532
00:23:53,519 --> 00:23:55,079
I can't even stand up for myself.

533
00:23:55,079 --> 00:23:55,920
Don't waste your gratitude.

534
00:23:57,119 --> 00:23:58,599
I was right outside the restroom earlier.

535
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:00,240
I heard you talking with Old Wei,

536
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,559
which was why I didn't go in.

537
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:03,960
Then why didn't you speak up?

538
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,640
If you're disappointed, say it.

539
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:07,039
If you think it's unfair, raise hell!

540
00:24:07,039 --> 00:24:08,240
What's the point of bottling it all up?

541
00:24:08,240 --> 00:24:09,519
There's nothing to bottle up.

542
00:24:09,519 --> 00:24:11,640
I never thought this honor would belong to me.

543
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:12,839
I don't deserve it.

544
00:24:15,119 --> 00:24:15,960
Be honest.

545
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,640
Tell me what you're really thinking, then.

546
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:22,759
Wen Zongshu and Lin Kanshan.

547
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:24,359
I'll keep my eyes locked on both of them.

548
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:25,920
Once I bring them in,

549
00:24:26,119 --> 00:24:27,920
let's see who has any excuse not to promote me.

550
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:50,200
You're here.

551
00:24:50,559 --> 00:24:51,160
Good evening.

552
00:25:32,559 --> 00:25:33,279
You're here.

553
00:25:34,079 --> 00:25:35,240
Has Director Guan been by?

554
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,160
What did they say after the consultation?

555
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:41,240
Same as last time.

556
00:25:41,519 --> 00:25:42,799
It's up to the family to decide.

557
00:25:51,759 --> 00:25:52,920
The director said

558
00:25:53,119 --> 00:25:54,240
if we opt for surgery,

559
00:25:54,559 --> 00:25:55,720
we have to decide early.

560
00:25:56,319 --> 00:25:58,039
We need to book the OR in advance, too.

561
00:25:58,240 --> 00:25:59,960
But he just had abdominal surgery,

562
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:01,440
and at his age,

563
00:26:01,839 --> 00:26:03,319
can he handle two surgeries?

564
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:19,559
Eat well.

565
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:24,839
If you're tired, get some proper sleep there.

566
00:26:25,039 --> 00:26:26,119
Don't wear yourself out too.

567
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,160
Where's the little pot I bought?

568
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:33,960
Aren't you making porridge if you get hungry at night?

569
00:26:34,599 --> 00:26:35,960
I put it away.

570
00:26:36,559 --> 00:26:37,759
The old man said the fumes bothered him.

571
00:26:37,759 --> 00:26:39,119
He won't let me cook in the room.

572
00:26:39,759 --> 00:26:41,119
He has a bad temper.

573
00:26:41,119 --> 00:26:42,839
Last time, he almost threw the pot out.

574
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:47,000
Let me ask around again

575
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:48,400
to see if surgery is better

576
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:50,039
or conservative treatment.

577
00:27:19,559 --> 00:27:20,400
Director Yin!

578
00:27:21,279 --> 00:27:22,519
Where are you kicking back today?

579
00:27:23,039 --> 00:27:24,680
When will you make good on that meal you promised?

580
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:26,119
Won't you even give me some face?

581
00:27:26,119 --> 00:27:27,359
I'm totally embarrassed here.

582
00:27:28,279 --> 00:27:29,599
It's not my treat,

583
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:31,720
it's Director Qian Xinfu.

584
00:27:32,319 --> 00:27:34,119
His own father is staying in your hospital.

585
00:27:34,119 --> 00:27:35,720
He wouldn't dare not toast you.

586
00:27:37,039 --> 00:27:38,200
Oh, by the way,

587
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:40,160
could you help arrange a private room?

588
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:42,119
My mom doesn't mind either way.

589
00:27:42,319 --> 00:27:44,240
Her brain tumor is pressing on some nerve,

590
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:45,559
so she just wants to sleep all day.

591
00:27:45,559 --> 00:27:46,920
Old Mr. Qian can't sleep well,

592
00:27:47,279 --> 00:27:48,519
complaining to his son every day.

593
00:27:48,519 --> 00:27:49,200
If this isn't sorted out

594
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:50,359
and he finds an excuse to make trouble,

595
00:27:50,359 --> 00:27:51,319
you won't like it either.

596
00:27:51,839 --> 00:27:53,160
I'm at the hospital right now.

597
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:55,359
The old man could barely breathe just now.

598
00:27:57,559 --> 00:27:58,359
Why don't you check on it?

599
00:27:59,400 --> 00:27:59,880
Alright.

600
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:01,400
I'll wait for your word, then.

601
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:02,559
Bye, bye.

602
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:11,640
Uncle Zhang, I'm heading out!

603
00:28:11,759 --> 00:28:13,400
Alright, take care!

604
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:17,200
Uncle Zhang, got my cousin's money order?

605
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,640
Oh, it's you. Check inside the box.

606
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:19,359
If it's there, it's there.

607
00:28:19,359 --> 00:28:20,119
If not, it's not.

608
00:28:32,119 --> 00:28:34,119
What about the parcel from Xiamen?

609
00:28:34,119 --> 00:28:35,359
Nothing at all!

610
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:37,799
There haven't been any packages for you lately.

611
00:28:38,799 --> 00:28:39,640
Thanks anyway.

612
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:41,240
Take care now.

613
00:28:44,559 --> 00:28:45,799
Dad, I'm home.

614
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:52,400
What time is it? You haven't eaten yet?

615
00:28:52,839 --> 00:28:53,920
Who are you looking for?

616
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:00,440
What's wrong?

617
00:29:01,160 --> 00:29:01,839
It's me...

618
00:29:01,839 --> 00:29:04,039
I asked who you are.

619
00:29:04,559 --> 00:29:07,759
Who are you looking for at this hour?

620
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:08,839
Who are you looking for?

621
00:29:09,079 --> 00:29:10,200
Calm down, don't get agitated.

622
00:29:12,119 --> 00:29:13,000
She's your daughter.

623
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:14,440
Take a breath.

624
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:16,119
Why doesn't he recognize me?

625
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,319
He's getting more and more confused.

626
00:29:18,640 --> 00:29:19,400
It's just today.

627
00:29:20,319 --> 00:29:21,440
He has good days and bad days.

628
00:29:21,680 --> 00:29:23,039
Maybe he'll be fine tomorrow.

629
00:29:23,759 --> 00:29:25,759
Did you give him the imported medicine?

630
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,359
It's all gone.

631
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:28,720
The new batch hasn't arrived yet.

632
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:30,960
There's another dish on the stove.

633
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:35,039
Where's your brother?

634
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:37,400
Why isn't he back yet?

635
00:29:38,079 --> 00:29:39,559
Call him.

636
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:42,119
The soup is getting cold.

637
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:45,319
Did you hear what I said?

638
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,200
Call him!

639
00:29:47,319 --> 00:29:49,000
Call him right now!

640
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:52,240
Call him! Give him a call!

641
00:29:52,519 --> 00:29:54,400
Your son is in prison!

642
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,559
If you want to see him, you must eat properly!

643
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:57,799
Stay alive!

644
00:30:07,319 --> 00:30:08,319
Stay alive!

645
00:30:08,319 --> 00:30:08,880
Live...

646
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:17,160
Live until he gets out!

647
00:30:20,039 --> 00:30:20,720
Sis, Sis, Sis.

648
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:21,759
Let me. Let me do it.

649
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:23,440
Here, give it to me. Give it to me.

650
00:30:24,640 --> 00:30:25,720
Don't be angry.

651
00:30:26,759 --> 00:30:28,319
It's okay, don't be mad. Come on.

652
00:30:33,799 --> 00:30:34,720
Don't be upset now.

653
00:30:36,279 --> 00:30:37,359
Come on, let's eat first.

654
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:38,200
Eat properly.

655
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:39,559
Brother will be back soon.

656
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:45,759
We need to keep you healthy,

657
00:30:46,279 --> 00:30:48,359
so you'll be happy when he's back, right?

658
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:51,920
Have some soup to wash it down.

659
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:53,240
Slowly. Careful, it's hot.

660
00:31:01,039 --> 00:31:01,720
Sis.

661
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,000
Brother-in-law should be back soon, right?

662
00:31:08,519 --> 00:31:09,759
He's been away on this trip long enough.

663
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,400
It must've been several years now.

664
00:31:23,279 --> 00:31:23,960
Sis,

665
00:31:24,279 --> 00:31:25,319
about my husband's situation,

666
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:26,880
did you ask about it?

667
00:31:27,680 --> 00:31:28,720
What situation?

668
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:33,240
If it's too much trouble, never mind.

669
00:31:34,119 --> 00:31:36,880
The other party just took it to court.

670
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:37,720
The court hasn't ruled yet.

671
00:31:38,359 --> 00:31:39,160
I'd like to try

672
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,039
asking around once more.

673
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:45,519
What did the county traffic police say?

674
00:31:46,119 --> 00:31:47,319
How will it be classified in the end?

675
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:49,680
Hit-and-run, or a traffic accident?

676
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,240
No one knows.

677
00:31:51,839 --> 00:31:53,319
We don't even know who to ask.

678
00:31:56,839 --> 00:31:57,880
Is the other person out of the hospital?

679
00:31:58,279 --> 00:31:59,920
What if... what if we settle privately?

680
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:00,680
How much do they want?

681
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:02,720
18,000.

682
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:04,319
Not counting lost wages.

683
00:32:19,599 --> 00:32:21,359
The eggs are a bit salty.

684
00:32:32,359 --> 00:32:34,119
Just rest easy

685
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:35,640
and stay right here.

686
00:32:35,640 --> 00:32:36,759
I'll figure something out.

687
00:32:39,160 --> 00:32:40,480
Taste it and see if it's too salty.

688
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:27,799
Hey, old classmate, it's Li Fengge.

689
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,799
Not on duty at the detention center today?

690
00:33:34,799 --> 00:33:36,559
Just asking about the sentence reduction.

691
00:33:37,359 --> 00:33:38,920
Still haven't heard any news?

692
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:42,119
No.

693
00:33:43,160 --> 00:33:44,640
My dad misses his son.

694
00:33:45,359 --> 00:33:46,359
He keeps pushing me to ask.

695
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:48,319
I already told him,

696
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:49,960
the law is the law.

697
00:33:50,279 --> 00:33:51,720
It's not that simple.

698
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:52,960
Regardless of the reason,

699
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:55,160
but the old man's health right now...

700
00:34:00,079 --> 00:34:00,880
I understand.

701
00:34:01,519 --> 00:34:03,119
Let me know as soon as you hear anything.

702
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:04,319
Will do.

703
00:34:24,320 --> 00:34:25,079
What if we settle privately?

704
00:34:25,079 --> 00:34:26,079
How much do they want?

705
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:27,599
18,000.

706
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:29,440
Not including lost wages.

707
00:34:55,840 --> 00:34:57,440
Please page 49013.

708
00:34:58,719 --> 00:34:59,519
Last name Li.

709
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:01,480
Ask him to call back immediately.

710
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:14,519
Xiao Lin!

711
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:16,519
It's me.

712
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:17,480
Don't you remember?

713
00:35:17,880 --> 00:35:19,760
You followed me from the school to here,

714
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:20,880
following me for so long,

715
00:35:21,159 --> 00:35:22,320
and I still don't know your last name

716
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:23,239
or what to call you.

717
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:25,360
My last name is Lin! Xiao Lin!

718
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:26,840
I've been looking for you.

719
00:35:27,199 --> 00:35:28,360
Where have you been all these years?

720
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:30,519
You passed the school gate this morning,

721
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:32,039
didn't you? Right?

722
00:35:32,159 --> 00:35:33,360
I knew I wasn't mistaken.

723
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:34,639
You've got the wrong person.

724
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,119
I didn't know you were coming.

725
00:36:19,719 --> 00:36:20,719
I got back a bit late.

726
00:36:21,639 --> 00:36:23,079
The mainland really toughens people up.

727
00:36:23,360 --> 00:36:24,719
Your tolerance has really gone up.

728
00:36:24,719 --> 00:36:27,840
You're no longer the lightweight Xiao Lin.

729
00:36:28,719 --> 00:36:29,960
I haven't been back in years,

730
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:31,519
so I caught up with an old classmate.

731
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:33,360
Isn't that just Chen Leyuan?

732
00:36:33,639 --> 00:36:34,800
Some classmate.

733
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,519
Right now in Taipei, besides him,

734
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:38,440
can you even find another friend?

735
00:36:41,079 --> 00:36:43,440
I just learned you made division chief.

736
00:36:43,639 --> 00:36:44,719
Let me toast you with tea instead of wine.

737
00:36:44,719 --> 00:36:45,639
My sincere congratulations.

738
00:36:48,679 --> 00:36:51,760
Let's drop the formalities between us.

739
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,000
The reason I'm here

740
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,800
is to hear the truth.

741
00:36:55,079 --> 00:36:57,599
Let out all your grievances.

742
00:37:01,599 --> 00:37:03,079
This is your only chance.

743
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:07,320
If you don't speak, I won't either at tomorrow's meeting.

744
00:37:07,519 --> 00:37:08,840
Once I retire,

745
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:09,880
believe it or not,

746
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:11,920
there won't be a single person left

747
00:37:11,920 --> 00:37:12,880
to speak for you on the front line.

748
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:23,079
So many people have been sent to the mainland.

749
00:37:23,239 --> 00:37:24,880
Can't you treat everyone fairly?

750
00:37:25,199 --> 00:37:26,679
Those slackers,

751
00:37:26,679 --> 00:37:28,639
they're thriving every single day,

752
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:30,639
with endless operational funds.

753
00:37:31,360 --> 00:37:33,159
They spend six months there and return decorated.

754
00:37:33,159 --> 00:37:33,880
Coming and going as they please,

755
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:34,920
whenever they want.

756
00:37:35,199 --> 00:37:36,400
Why do some of us have to

757
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:38,440
be left to fend for ourselves like weeds?

758
00:37:39,239 --> 00:37:39,960
Go on.

759
00:37:40,480 --> 00:37:42,039
We crossed the sea,

760
00:37:43,239 --> 00:37:45,920
surrounded by guns and watchful eyes,

761
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:47,519
wasting away for years.

762
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:50,280
Some never even make it back.

763
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:51,480
Someone like me got lucky.

764
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:53,920
I return to find even my ID was changed.

765
00:37:53,920 --> 00:37:55,039
Ancestral home is ancestral home.

766
00:37:55,039 --> 00:37:56,360
Why insist on changing it to birthplace?

767
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:59,039
Changing Zhangzhou to Kaohsiung.

768
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:01,000
I still have to find my grandaunt there.

769
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:03,280
Lee Teng-hui has wiped out our very roots!

770
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:04,039
Fine.

771
00:38:04,320 --> 00:38:05,679
I don't care about the ID card.

772
00:38:05,679 --> 00:38:06,280
What about the rest?

773
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:08,159
Under the Communists' noses in Minzhong,

774
00:38:08,159 --> 00:38:09,039
I was stealing intelligence,

775
00:38:09,039 --> 00:38:11,320
while politicians here hold pressers,

776
00:38:11,760 --> 00:38:13,039
right in front of reporters,

777
00:38:13,039 --> 00:38:14,840
publicly selling out our own people!

778
00:38:15,239 --> 00:38:16,280
Whether we live or die...

779
00:38:16,280 --> 00:38:17,480
they didn't give a damn!

780
00:38:17,480 --> 00:38:18,480
Aren't we human beings?

781
00:38:18,559 --> 00:38:20,000
Do we deserve to die?

782
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:21,039
If it were me—

783
00:38:29,119 --> 00:38:30,199
Does anyone else

784
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:32,119
know you're back?

785
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:34,880
Just my dad.

786
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:37,679
I call him once a week.

787
00:38:38,760 --> 00:38:39,960
He's the only one who knows.

788
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:45,119
Answer it.

789
00:38:50,559 --> 00:38:51,239
Dad.

790
00:38:52,320 --> 00:38:53,880
I got back the day before yesterday.

791
00:38:54,639 --> 00:38:55,960
I still have some work to finish.

792
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:57,119
I'll visit you in a couple of days.

793
00:38:57,800 --> 00:38:59,360
Do you want to visit Mom's grave?

794
00:39:00,320 --> 00:39:01,519
Alright, alright.

795
00:39:02,760 --> 00:39:04,800
I still have unfinished business here.

796
00:39:06,559 --> 00:39:07,760
I haven't forgotten Grandaunt.

797
00:39:07,760 --> 00:39:08,800
I'm still looking for her.

798
00:39:11,440 --> 00:39:13,000
We'll talk more when I see you.

799
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:13,960
Talk to you later.

800
00:39:14,199 --> 00:39:15,119
Go to bed early, okay?

801
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:23,079
What else?

802
00:39:26,119 --> 00:39:28,639
I heard a lot of rumors after returning.

803
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:32,199
They say you're ill and unwell,

804
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:33,519
and that you're about to retire.

805
00:39:34,760 --> 00:39:37,239
My issues can wait for now.

806
00:39:38,519 --> 00:39:39,599
You've always treated me best.

807
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:42,719
I hope you'll always be my superior.

808
00:39:43,239 --> 00:39:45,280
In the entire MIB, top to bottom,

809
00:39:46,320 --> 00:39:47,760
the only person I truly respect

810
00:39:48,119 --> 00:39:49,079
is you.

811
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:51,119
To be honest,

812
00:39:52,559 --> 00:39:53,920
I don't really mind.

813
00:39:55,679 --> 00:39:57,039
But if I retire,

814
00:39:57,800 --> 00:39:59,639
Taiwan, China's intel network will fall.

815
00:39:59,639 --> 00:40:01,159
And I can't accept that.

816
00:40:02,599 --> 00:40:04,039
Don't listen to those rumors.

817
00:40:05,360 --> 00:40:07,239
It's just unstable blood pressure.

818
00:40:07,599 --> 00:40:08,280
It won't kill me.

819
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:12,800
I will report everything you told me.

820
00:40:14,039 --> 00:40:15,519
Just focus on your job,

821
00:40:15,519 --> 00:40:16,800
and leave the rest to me.

822
00:40:18,400 --> 00:40:19,360
Get some rest.

823
00:40:20,559 --> 00:40:21,199
Wait a second.

824
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:22,519
Hold on a moment.

825
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,960
A boss has to wear a gold watch.

826
00:40:36,599 --> 00:40:37,559
Once you're in the mainland,

827
00:40:38,599 --> 00:40:39,440
run your business well,

828
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:40,519
be a decent man.

829
00:40:40,719 --> 00:40:42,519
And when you return to report one day,

830
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:44,719
you'll give me an even more expensive one.

831
00:40:45,079 --> 00:40:47,159
If you amount to nothing,

832
00:40:47,159 --> 00:40:49,920
it just means Old Zhu here misjudged you.

833
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:54,039
Back when I left for the mainland,

834
00:40:54,039 --> 00:40:55,679
that's what you told me the day you saw me off.

835
00:41:07,400 --> 00:41:10,800
I heard you've been giving out gifts since you got back.

836
00:41:12,239 --> 00:41:15,000
You gave Liqing a box of Changbai ginseng.

837
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:17,079
Is money that easy to make on the mainland?

838
00:41:17,239 --> 00:41:18,880
Those were all fake.

839
00:41:19,559 --> 00:41:21,000
The roots snapped as soon as you pinched them,

840
00:41:21,400 --> 00:41:23,320
I had to glue them back together myself.

841
00:42:14,239 --> 00:42:16,079
Still trying to crack Lin Kanshan's email password?

842
00:42:16,400 --> 00:42:17,320
Both SIM cards are encrypted.

843
00:42:17,599 --> 00:42:18,840
Can't crack them any time soon.

844
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:20,440
I can only try my luck with his email.

845
00:42:21,199 --> 00:42:21,920
What about you?

846
00:42:22,280 --> 00:42:23,400
What's on your mind?

847
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:26,639
You suspect someone,

848
00:42:27,079 --> 00:42:28,760
but they've never suspected you.

849
00:42:29,559 --> 00:42:30,159
Right?

850
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:59,840
You tell me, us staying here every day,

851
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:02,719
what's the point of it?

852
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:09,559
I'm Wang Kai,

853
00:43:09,559 --> 00:43:11,280
inviting you to watch the TV drama

854
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:12,119
"Confrontation."

855
00:43:12,400 --> 00:43:14,039
What do we do? Should we leave now?

856
00:43:14,039 --> 00:43:15,400
If we let these few punks intimidate us,

857
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,400
we can forget about surviving out here.

858
00:43:16,400 --> 00:43:17,079
Get him!

859
00:43:18,599 --> 00:43:19,679
You really dare make a move?!

860
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:22,440
You're very close to Wen Zongshu.

861
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:23,400
Exactly how close?

862
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:25,480
Close enough to lend each other money.

863
00:43:25,480 --> 00:43:27,000
The second one is a pinhole camera.

864
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:28,000
The picture is clear,

865
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:29,519
and it can also record audio.

866
00:43:29,519 --> 00:43:30,800
I'll give you two addresses.

867
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:31,800
Run an on-site check.

868
00:43:32,199 --> 00:43:33,400
For the wiretap recordings,

869
00:43:33,400 --> 00:43:35,599
restrict access to me alone.
